MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug would give my recently purchased Echo Dot and Echo Show a useful new job: controlling a lamp through Alexa.",
    "The portable Seagate drive could complement my older desktop backup drive by letting me move files and keep another backup."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV sticks and older Echo models repeat functions covered by my recent 4K Max, fourth-generation Echo Dot and Echo Show purchases, without giving me a clear reason to add them.",
    "The USB 2.0 hub feels unnecessary because my card reader already adds USB 3.0 ports. The earbuds, tablet and Bluetooth speaker do not address a current need I have identified."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying Alexa devices seems to have been taken as a reason to recommend more Alexa devices, even when they would duplicate what I just bought.",
    "My history of buying computer accessories seems to have been treated as interest in any accessory, without enough attention to whether it adds a useful capability."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter because they show which needs I have already covered, especially when the suggested item is an older version of something I now have.",
    "I have reasons to buy complementary items, such as a stand for my Echo Show or a replacement battery for my Harmony remote. That kind of specific connection matters more to me than simply sharing a brand or function."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in practical home electronics but often confused extending my setup with duplicating devices I already have."
}
